  "id": "eps",
  "term": "EPS",
  "definition": "EPS, or extrapyramidal syndrome, is a group of movement problems caused by dysfunction in brain motor pathways that help control muscle tone, posture, and coordinated movement. It can include dystonia, akathisia, parkinsonism-like slowing and tremor, and tardive dyskinesia with involuntary movements, and may arise in neurological conditions or as a medication side effect.",
